{"results": [{"id": "hp_doc_cd702ba07d8c20084c905b7370d3a246d60534d6adb27a0985883fd1274e4955", "title": "Celtic Woman: A Celtic Family Christmas", "text": "Celtic Woman: A Celtic Family Christmas is a collaborative album by the group Celtic Woman and The High Kings, released on October 14, 2008.", "score": 52.7635}, {"id": "hp_doc_b46da6a0942e9dd034361b565632afaf6b39c4a09cf4591f8f6844c1cc9f377e", "title": "Celtic Woman: Silent Night", "text": "Celtic Woman: Silent Night is a Christmas compilation album by Celtic Woman. Along with \"\", it was released on October 9, 2012. This is their first album to be distributed by EMI Music Christian Music Group (CMG Distribution), initially an exclusive CD available at Christian retailers. It has since become available through other outlets. \"Silent Night\" features a brand new song, “The Light Of Christmas Morn,” performed by Chloë Agnew and Lisa Lambe. The other tracks have been drawn from their first Christmas album \"A Christmas Celebration\", which was released in 2006.", "score": 38.5942}, {"id": "hp_doc_940f4202e21b256e41b0d54a295995c96993584ea139648b6e67875281339deb", "title": "Celtic Woman: A New Journey", "text": "Celtic Woman: A New Journey is the second on-stage production by the group Celtic Woman. The show was filmed at Slane Castle in County Meath, Ireland and featured Hayley Westenra as a new addition to the group. The album was released on 30 January 2007. This album broke a long-standing record when it surpassed the 81-week run of the original \"Celtic Woman\" album. The Celtic Woman performers change their outfits at least three times.", "score": 34.5309}], "remaining_searches": 2}
